  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "05. Attack Sequence",
    "ruleNumber": "05.03",
    "order": 98,
    "anchor": "05.03",
    "summary": "The opposing player resolves 3 steps:\n\n1. Create Groups: split the target unit's models into groups.\n2. Allocation Order: fix the sequence in which groups take attacks.\n3. Make Save Rolls: roll 1 D6 per wounding attack, as its **save roll**.\n\nGroups are formed as often as needed:\n\n- each **CHARACTER** model is its own group\n- all other models sharing W, Sv and InSv form 1 group\n\nThe order fixed in step 2 must meet all of these:\n\n- a non-**CHARACTER** group containing a wounded model goes first\n- every non-**CHARACTER** group comes before every **CHARACTER** group\n- **CHARACTER** groups with a wounded model come before **CHARACTER** groups with none",
    "citations": [
      {
